@baseUrl = http://localhost:5128
@HostAddress = {{baseUrl}}
@superAdminEmail = admin@amanix.com
@superAdminPassword = Admin@123456
@companyAdminEmail = admin@al-salamah.com
@companyAdminPassword = User@123456
@missingTenant = 3f9a1c22-7b44-4e18-9d05-6c2e8a5f1b70
@missingPlan = 6b2e8a5f-1b70-4e18-9d05-3f9a1c227b44

### =====================================================================
### 17. SUBSCRIPTION TIERS, QUOTAS AND EXPIRY (FR-SUB)
### =====================================================================
### Plans are data: platform staff create and reprice them, and a company's limits are read
### through the plan it is linked to rather than copied onto it. A quota left null is unlimited.
###
### A company's standing is derived, never stored: Active → GracePeriod → ReadOnly, computed
### from the expiry date and the plan's grace days. Grace still writes; ReadOnly refuses writes
### with 402 while every read, export and sign-in keeps working.
###
### A company with no plan on file is UNGOVERNED — unlimited and never expiring. That is what
### made this feature safe to deploy onto a platform that already had live customers.
###
### The state machine, the quota arithmetic, the seat-counting rules and the middleware's
### exemptions are covered by SubscriptionGovernanceTests and
### SubscriptionEnforcementMiddlewareTests (xUnit). This suite is a smoke test of the surface
### with explicit assertions. Field casing is camelCase (D-8).

### 17.1 Platform SuperAdmin login
# @name superAdminLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "email": "{{superAdminEmail}}", "password": "{{superAdminPassword}}" }

?? status == 200

@superAdminToken = {{superAdminLogin.data.token}}

### 17.2 Company Admin login
# @name companyAdminLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "email": "{{companyAdminEmail}}", "password": "{{companyAdminPassword}}" }

?? status == 200

@companyAdminToken = {{companyAdminLogin.data.token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### The public price list
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 17.3 Anonymous pricing page -> 200, and the seeded catalogue is there
### Public because the sign-up page needs it before anyone has an account.
# @name publicPlans
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/subscription-plans
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.data.length > 3

### 17.4 Enterprise sells unlimited, and says so with null rather than a large number
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/subscription-plans
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.data.filter(p => p.code.startsWith('ENTERPRISE') && p.maxStaffUsers != null).length < 1
?? js response.parsedBody.data.filter(p => p.code.startsWith('STARTER') && p.maxStaffUsers > 9).length > 0

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Authentication and authorization
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 17.5 Unauthenticated read of one's own subscription -> 401
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/tenants/subscription

?? status == 401

### 17.6 Unauthenticated platform catalogue -> 401
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans

?? status == 401

### 17.7 A company admin cannot reach the platform catalogue -> 403
### Raising your own limits is not a tenant capability.
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 403

### 17.8 A company admin cannot assign itself a plan -> 403
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/tenants/{{missingTenant}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "planCode": "ENTERPRISE", "termMonths": 120 }

?? status == 403

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### The company's own view
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 17.9 A company admin reads its own subscription -> 200, with every quota listed
### The seeded companies are on no plan, so this is the ungoverned shape a frontend must handle.
# @name mySubscription
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/tenants/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200
?? body data.writesPermitted == true
?? js response.parsedBody.data.quotas.length > 2
?? js response.parsedBody.data.quotas.filter(q => q.limit != null).length < 1

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Plan administration
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 17.10 The platform catalogue includes retired plans -> 200
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.data.length > 3

### 17.11 A plan code that is already taken -> 409
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "code": "STARTER",
  "nameAr": "مكرر",
  "nameEn": "Duplicate",
  "monthlyPriceSar": 100,
  "annualPriceSar": 1000,
  "trialDays": 0,
  "graceDays": 7,
  "displayOrder": 9
}

?? status == 409

### 17.12 A quota of zero -> 400
### Unlimited is expressed by omitting the field; 0 would be a plan that permits nothing.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "code": "ZERO-SEATS",
  "nameAr": "صفر",
  "nameEn": "Zero",
  "monthlyPriceSar": 100,
  "annualPriceSar": 1000,
  "maxStaffUsers": 0,
  "trialDays": 0,
  "graceDays": 7,
  "displayOrder": 9
}

?? status == 400

### 17.13 A grace period longer than the sanity ceiling -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "code": "FOREVER-GRACE",
  "nameAr": "مهلة",
  "nameEn": "Grace",
  "monthlyPriceSar": 100,
  "annualPriceSar": 1000,
  "trialDays": 0,
  "graceDays": 9999,
  "displayOrder": 9
}

?? status == 400

### 17.14 A plan code with spaces in it -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "code": "not a code",
  "nameAr": "رمز",
  "nameEn": "Code",
  "monthlyPriceSar": 100,
  "annualPriceSar": 1000,
  "trialDays": 0,
  "graceDays": 7,
  "displayOrder": 9
}

?? status == 400

### 17.15 Editing a plan that does not exist -> 404
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans/{{missingPlan}}
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "code": "GHOST",
  "nameAr": "غير موجود",
  "nameEn": "Ghost",
  "monthlyPriceSar": 100,
  "annualPriceSar": 1000,
  "trialDays": 0,
  "graceDays": 7,
  "displayOrder": 9
}

?? status == 404

### 17.16 Retiring a plan that does not exist -> 404
PATCH {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscription-plans/{{missingPlan}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "isActive": false }

?? status == 404

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Assigning a company to a plan
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 17.17 The renewal worklist -> 200
### Ungoverned companies first: a company nobody put on a tier is invisible everywhere else,
### precisely because nothing refuses it anything.
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200

### 17.18 Only the companies on no plan -> 200
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/subscriptions?ungovernedOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.data.filter(t => t.planId != null).length < 1

### 17.19 Reading a company that does not exist -> 404
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/tenants/{{missingTenant}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404

### 17.20 Assigning a plan that does not exist -> 404
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/tenants/{{missingTenant}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "planCode": "NO-SUCH-PLAN", "termMonths": 12 }

?? status == 404

### 17.21 Both a term and an end date -> 400
### Two ways of saying when the term ends is an instruction the server would have to guess at.
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/tenants/{{missingTenant}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "planCode": "STARTER", "termMonths": 12, "expiresAtUtc": "2027-01-01T00:00:00Z" }

?? status == 400

### 17.22 A trial with a term attached -> 400
### A trial takes its length from the plan, so a term alongside it means the caller believes
### one thing and the system would do another.
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/tenants/{{missingTenant}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "planCode": "STARTER", "termMonths": 12, "startTrial": true }

?? status == 400

### 17.23 A term longer than the ten-year ceiling -> 400
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/tenants/{{missingTenant}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "planCode": "STARTER", "termMonths": 600 }

?? status == 400

### 17.24 A trial on a company that does not exist -> 404
### The plan resolves, the company does not, and "there is no such company" is the more useful
### answer than anything about the trial. That ENTERPRISE offers no trial at all is asserted by
### SubscriptionGovernanceTests.StartingATrialOnAPlanThatHasNone_IsRefused, which can set up a
### real company to prove it.
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/platform/tenants/{{missingTenant}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "planCode": "ENTERPRISE", "startTrial": true }

?? status == 404
